  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on preferring the more right-skewed lottery (i.e., more probability on unfavorable outcomes). Lottery A is more right-skewed (90% unfavorable) than B (45% unfavorable), so the reason would favor A. However, the individual chose B, which is less right-skewed, and justified this by emphasizing the higher chance of avoiding loss (55% vs 10%), which reflects a preference for better odds of a favorable outcome — the opposite of favoring right-skewness. The individual considered the probabilities of favorable and unfavorable outcomes, which aligns with information relevant to skewness. However, their decision rule — preferring higher chance of avoiding loss — contradicts the skewness-based rule, which would favor more concentration on unfavorable outcomes. Thus, while some relevant information is considered, the justification and decision rule are inconsistent with the decision reason. The individual appears to avoid right-skewness rather than prefer it.",
